meta {
  name: 04-iam-journey
  seq: 5
}

docs {
  The IAM building blocks, assembled the way the domain intends: create a
  permission, bundle it into a policy, create a group, attach the policy, then
  add a user. Runs as `admin`.

  The payoff is the last request, which proves the chain actually grants
  something: `other` gains a permission purely by being added to the group.
  Each link in isolation would prove very little.

  Names are suffixed with a per-run value because permissions, policies, and
  groups are unique by name and this suite must be re-runnable against a
  database that already holds the previous run's records.
}
